Three forces act on an object. If the object is in translational equilibrium, which of the following must be true?

1. The vector sum of the 3 forces must be equal to zero;
2. the magnitudes of the 3 forces must be equal;
3. all the 3 forces must be acting at the same point.

One end of a horizontal string is fixed to a wall. It is then plucked transversely at a point 3/4 way from the wall, as shown in Figure 8. Which of the following refers to the correct property of the wave after it reflects off the wall?

![fig-8](gce-al-physics-2020-p1-officiel-cameroun_exercice_1_fig_8.png)

1) It has a greater speed after it reflects on the wall;
2) It has a greater frequency after it reflects off the wall;
3) The reflected pulse will be a trough.

A train with a long steel axle is moving eastwards. Which of the following statements is / are true about this train?

1) An emf is induced across the axle, which is proportional to the velocity of the train;
2) The vertical component of the earth's magnetic field contributes to the voltage induced across the axle;
3) There is no induced current in the axle of the train.

*Options as printed:* A) 1 and 2 are correct   B) 2 and 3 are correct   C) 1 only is correct   D) 3 only is correct
